{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "How to Write a Work Plan"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about work plan design."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Learning Outcome"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through grammar and vocabulary structures.  Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic programming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Continuous for Plans in Affirmative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>The<strong> present continuous</strong> is also used to talk about short term plans, or arrangements.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>We normally use the <strong>present continuous</strong> to talk about things happening at the moment, but we can also use it to express plans we have in the near future. We just need to add a future time expression (tomorrow, next Saturday) instead of a current present expression (now, right now) to differentiate them. </p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>I&rsquo;<strong>m designing</strong> the software now. (present) </i></p> <p><i>We&rsquo;<strong>re recording</strong> the interviews tomorrow. (future)</i></p> <p>Remember to use the verb <i>to be</i> plus the main verb in its <i>-ing</i> form:&nbsp;</p> <p>The <strong>present continuous</strong> is used for future plans when we talk about activities that are taking place only in the near future. </p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"PRESENT CONTINOUS\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"PRESENT\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"NEAR FUTURE\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul> <li><i>The developer <strong>is analyzing</strong> the requirements now.</i></li> <li><i>The debate <strong>is taking </strong>place right now.</i></li> <li><i>The software<strong> is taking</strong> too long in arriving.</i></li> </ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul> <li><i>We <strong>are sorting out </strong>the requirements <u>later</u>. </i></li> <li><i>The report <strong>is arriving </strong><u>next weekend</u>.</i></li> <li><i>The company <strong>is sending</strong> the software <u>tomorrow</u>.</i></li> </ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Brainstorming some ideas and writing them down is a good way to establish more clearly the goals you are achieving."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Make sure you include specific information about how you're fulfilling these objectives, describing every single necessary action."}, {"type": "example", "content": "No matter where your project is going, you need serious support and resources to complete it."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "How to Improve Your Writing Skills"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>Writing can be difficult, especially when you are not used to write quite often. There are some guidelines that can help you <strong>improve your skills</strong> at the moment of writing.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>You can use the next tips to improve your writing skills:</p> <p><strong>Brush up on the basics:</strong> when you write, make sure you check carefully the structures you use. A good grammar book or blog may help you check your statements.</p> <p><strong>Find a writing partner:</strong> probably there is a person at your work place or college, who wants to improve his/her skills as well; look for that person and become pen pals, start exchanging your work to have feedback and improve together.</p> <p><strong>Join a workshop:</strong> you don&rsquo;t need to attend the best university in your area to learn how to write, but try to get a night class, or a workshop. A writing class may help you develop your abilities and to become a refined writer.</p> <p><strong>Write and read like it&rsquo;s your job:</strong> the best writers are also good readers, read as much as you can, and implement conscious reading; this is to look carefully at the sentences, the structure, turns of phrases, connectors and so on and so forth.</p> <p>Remember that practice creates masters, so write every day if possible, and check your writing to make your skills much better.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Remember to check your grammar and structures, you can use a reference grammar book to make sure you are writing correctly."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "outline"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "framework, skeleton"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A work plan is an outline of the reasons and steps for the development of a project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "schedule "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "time plan  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Use a tentative schedule to organize your strategy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "background "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "history, setting  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Secondly, write the introduction and background of your project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sign onto "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take part in something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The background is the reason why you are signing onto the project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "piecemeal "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "piece by piece  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Make sure you  write the strategy piecemeal."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fall behind "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be unable to finish something on time  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Remember to build space not to fall behind in your work.   "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research more about the steps to write a work plan.\t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a format that you consider useful to write a work plan. \t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a mini work plan for a week in a company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Expose your work to your instructor and partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I get information about a work plan. \t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I Design a format to write a work plan. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a mini work plan for a week. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my work with my instructor and partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le01ob06re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob06re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">It is very important for you to design a work plan in order to land your project and make it plausible. A work plan is an outline of the reasons and steps for the development of a project. In a work plan, you break down all your project into small tasks and organize them in a schedule. A work plan also permits your readers to understand what your project is about.\nNow, we are going to learn how to write a work plan. Remember to check your grammar and make sure you know how the structures work in the different tenses; you can use a reference grammar book to make sure you are writing correctly. Now, let's see the step by step to write a work plan.</div>"}, {"time": "51500", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob06re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">First of all, you have to consider the intention of your plan, this is what you are willing to achieve with your project. Think about it and set the purpose clearly. Brainstorming some ideas and writing them down is a good way to establish more clearly the goals you are achieving.\nSecondly, write the introduction and background of your project. In the introduction, explain briefly what your project is about and engage the readers to know more about it. The background is the reason why you are signing onto the project.\nThirdly, you need to write the goals and objectives of your project. The goals are the general aims you have, while the objectives are more specific and concrete targets. Make sure you include specific information about how you're fulfilling these objectives, describing every single necessary action. The next thing you have to do is list all the sources of information needed to complete your project. No matter where your project is going, you need serious support and resources to complete it.</div>"}, {"time": "131000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob06re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Then, identify possible constrains of your project, that is,  obstacles that may get in your way during its development. Once you identify these possible hinders, you can write a strategy to achieve your goals, and overcome them. Make sure you write the strategy piecemeal; use a tentative schedule to organize your strategy where you include every single thing you're doing, and remember to allocate additional time to keep you from falling behind in your work.</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le01ob06re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "template_override": 1, "id": 3, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n3le01ob06re5vsc01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can learn how to write a work plan."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can identify the steps to write a work plan."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can read about the importance of a work plan."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think a work plan is? And what's its content?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why do you think it is important to plan an activity?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"ty